# Force LF line endings for anything meant to run on Linux, regardless of
# any developer's local core.autocrlf setting -- a CRLF shebang line
# (#!/usr/bin/env bash\r) breaks with "bad interpreter" on the actual
# deploy target (deploy/setup_poller_host.sh runs on a Hetzner Ubuntu box,
# 2026-09-11), so this isn't optional the way it might be for most files.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
